pipeline.canary_logs_missing.message:
{{#is_alert}}**CRITICAL**: The heartbeat record emitted every minute by Fluent Bit did not arrive. Application "no data" alerts during this window are pipeline failures, not idleness.{{/is_alert}}
{{#is_warning}}**WARNING**: The heartbeat record emitted every minute by Fluent Bit did not arrive. Application "no data" alerts during this window are pipeline failures, not idleness.{{/is_warning}}
{{#is_no_data}}**NO DATA**: the monitored signal stopped arriving. Check the telemetry pipeline canary first (a broken pipeline looks like silence).{{/is_no_data}}
{{#is_recovery}}Recovered.{{/is_recovery}}

Service: `telemetry-pipeline` | env: `test` | team: `observability` | owner: obs@example.com | tier: critical

Troubleshooting:
1. Fluent Bit health: GET http://<fluent-bit>:2020/api/v2/health on the aggregator / DaemonSet / sidecars.
2. Check fluentbit_output_errors_total and retries below; 403 from Datadog = wrong API key or site.
3. Check egress (NAT/firewall) to the Datadog logs intake for the configured site.

Runbook: https://runbooks.example.com/pipeline#pipeline-canary

